/// PostgreSQL host for the ARPI reporting layer, optionally carrying a port, for
/// example localhost:5432. This is a NON-SECRET connection setting. The database
/// identity (arpi_reporter) and its password are never stored here or anywhere else in
/// this repository; they live in the Power BI credential store on the machine that
/// refreshes the model. Change this value in Transform data > Manage parameters.
expression ArpiServer = "localhost:5432" meta [IsParameterQuery=true, Type="Text", IsParameterQueryRequired=true]
	lineageTag: c8941245-fc87-5ebd-b958-c940c972f108

	annotation PBI_ResultType = Text

/// PostgreSQL database name holding the ARPI reporting schema, for example arpi_dev.
/// NON-SECRET. The model reads the reporting schema and nothing else; arpi_reporter
/// holds no privilege on raw, staging, warehouse or audit, which is enforced by the
/// database rather than by this parameter.
expression ArpiDatabase = "arpi_dev" meta [IsParameterQuery=true, Type="Text", IsParameterQueryRequired=true]
	lineageTag: c651e484-7541-573f-bad7-cecff8a42d07

	annotation PBI_ResultType = Text
